    "ls|LS17_S7_U_1": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 1 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 29.11.2021 \n \nCentrally Sponsored Educational Institutes in Maharashtra \n \n \n*1. SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n      SHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE: \n \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) a comprehensive list of Centrally sponsored educational institutes established in Maharashtra since  \nthe year 2014 containing the details such as the courses offered, number of students studied \nevery year, the number of teaching faculty and non-teaching staff, etc. in each institute; \n \n(b) the number of graduate students passed out from each institute along with the total budget \nsanctioned and released for the overall development of these institutes so far; \n \n(c) whether the Union Government has not released the total sanctioned funds for the purpose; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) the appropriate steps taken or proposed to be taken by the Government to release the rest of the \nfunds for the overall development of these institutes in Maharashtra? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n*** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS ( A) TO ( E) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 1 TO BE \nANSWERED ON 29.11.2021 REGARDING “CENTRALLY SPONSORED EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTES IN \nMAHARASHTRA” ASKED BY SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS AND SHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE. \n(a):  In the state of Maharashtra, 03 new Central Higher Educational Institutions i.e.  Indian Institute \nof Management  (IIM), Nagpur, Indian Institute of Information Technology (IIIT) , Pune and Indian \nInstitute of Information Technology (IIIT), Nagpur  have been established since the year 2014.  The \ndetails of courses offered, number of students studied every year, the number of teaching faculty and \nnon-teaching staff in these institutes are as below: \nS. No. Institute \nestablished \nsince 2014 \nYear of \nEstablishment \nCourses offered Annual Student Intake No. of \nteaching \nfaculty \nNo. of non- \nteaching \nstaff \n2015-\n16 \n2016-\n17 \n2017-\n18 \n2018-\n19 \n2019-\n20 \n2020-\n21 \n2021-22 \n1.  IIM \nNagpur \n2015 Post Graduate \nProgramme in \nManagement \n(PGP), Fellow \nProgramme in \nManagement \n(FPM) \n55 55 58 111 121 222 257 30 34 \n2.  IIIT Pune 2016 B.Tech \nM.Tech \nPh.D. \nNA* 58 95 83 217 248 29 (B.Tech \nadmission \nis under \nprocess) \n14 15 \n3.  IIIT Nagpur 2016 B.Tech  \nPh.D \nNA* 54 167 173 203 350 28 (B.Tech \nadmission \nis under \nprocess)  \n35 24 \n \n(b): The number of graduate students passed out from each institute , the total budget sanctioned \nand released for the overall development of these institutes are as below: \nNo. of students passed out in academic year 2016-17 to 2020-21:  \n \nBudget Sanctioned and Released during the financial year 2016-17 to 2021-22 \n* Not Applicable \n \n(c) to (e):  Funds are released to the institute s as per the requirement projected by them \nperiodically and within budgetary provision. \n*** \nS. No. Institute  Students passed out \n2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 \n1.  IIM Nagpur 53 54 55 108 120 \n2.  IIIT Pune NA* NA* NA* 53 106 \n3.  IIIT Nagpur NA* NA* NA* 48 150 \n \nS. No \nInstitute  Sanctioned Budget Released Budget  (in Crore) \n2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \n1.  IIM Nagpur 5 27.51 26.05 54.04 55.16 72.4 14 5 27.51 26.05 54.04 55.16 46.97 \n2.  IIIT Pune Recurring grant of Rs. 10 crore and non-recurring \ngrant of Rs. 64.00 crore for establishment. \nNA* 4  2.5  5.38  5.33 2.5 - \n3.  IIIT Nagpur Recurring grant of Rs. 10 crore and non-recurring \ngrant of Rs. 64.00 crore for establishment. \nNA* 7  9  23.15  15  14  2.85  ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_10": " \n \n \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.10 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 29.11.2021 \n \nKendriya Vidyalaya in Hardoi, Uttar Pradesh \n \n†*10. SHRI ASHOK KUMAR RAWAT:  \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n(a)  whether the Government proposes to establish a Kendriya \nVidyalaya in Sandila in Misrikh Parliamentary Constituency, Hardoi \ndistrict, Uttar Pradesh;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; and  \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n****** \n \n  \n\n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nTHE LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 1 0 RAISED BY SHRI \nASHOK KUMAR RAWAT , HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT TO \nBE ANSWERED ON 29/11/2021 REGARDING KENDRIYA \nVIDYALAYA IN HARDOI, UTTAR PRADESH.  \n \n \n(a) to (c) One Kendriya Vidyalaya (KV) is functioning at Hardoi, District \nHardoi, Uttar Pradesh. Opening of new KVs is a continuous process. \nProposals for opening of new KVs are considered only if sponsored by \nMinistries or Departments of the Government of India / State \nGovernments / Union Territories (UTs) Administrations and committing \nresources for setting up a new KV. The proposals received from various \nsponsoring authorities found fulfilling the mandatory pre -requisites for \nopening of new KVs have to compete with other such proposals under \nthe “Challenge Method” and also subject to approval of the compete nt \nauthority. \n \nKendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan has not received any proposal in the \nprescribed proforma for opening of a new KV at Sandila in Misrikh \nParliamentary Constituency, Hardoi district.  \n \n****** \n ",
