    "ls|LS17_S7_U_229": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *229  \nANSWERED ON 14TH DECEMBER 2021  \n  \nSCHEME FOR DEVELOPMENT OF FPIs \n  \n†*229. SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI: \n           SHRI KRUPAL BALAJI TUMANE: \n \nWill the Minister of Food Processing Industries be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the total number of various schemes being implemented by the Government in Maharashtra \nparticularly in Washim and Yavatmal districts and Ramtek in Nagpur district for the \ndevelopment of Food Processing Industries (FPIs) as on date; \n \n(b) whether the Government is facing any difficulties in implementation of the said schemes \nin the rural and urban areas of Maharashtra and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the details of measures taken/being taken to ensure effective implementation of various \nsuch schemes in  Maharashtra particularly in  Washim, Yavatmal   and Parbhani districts \nand Ramtek; \n \n(d)   whether financial,  technical  and  commercial assistance is being provided for the \nupgradation of FPIs and micro FPIs in Maharashtra particularly in Washim and Parbhani \ndistricts and Ramtek through Aatmanirbhar Bharat Abhiyaan; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n  \n \nANSWER \n  \n \nTHE MINISTER FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES  \n(SHRI PASHUPATI KUMAR PARAS) \n \n  \n(a) to (e):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO THE PARTS  (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.229 FOR ANSWER ON 14 TH  DECEMBER 2021 ABOUT \n“SCHEMES FOR DEVELOPMENT OF FPIs” \n \n(a): Ministry of Food Processing Industries is implementing three schemes for development of \nFood Processing Industries across the country including all parts of Maharashtra, namely –(i) \nCentral Sector Umbrella Scheme “ Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana (PMKSY)”, \ncomprising of 8 component schemes; (ii) Centrally sponsored “PM Formalisation of Micro Food \nProcessing Enterprises (PMFME)” Scheme & (iii) Central Sector “Production Linked Incentive \n(PLI) Scheme” for Food Processing Sector. A total of  153 projects have been approved in the state \nfor setting up of Food processing industries under PMKSY,    out of which 106 projects have \nalready been completed. Out of these 153 projects, 18 projects are located in Nagpur district and \n1project is  in Washim District. 3 projects have also  been approved under PLI scheme in Nagpur \nDistrict. \n \n(b):  No Sir. \n \n(c):  In order to further encourage participation of entrepreneurs of the region and smooth \nimplementation of the projects, Ministry has taken various measures, which include - (i) Creating \nawareness about its schemes; (ii) Application, evaluation and sanction of projects through online \nportal; (iii) Dashboard for monitoring the implementation of the projects; (iv) Regular review \nmeetings with the promoters/state nodal departments/  banks for speedy implementation; (v) \nAssessing the progress of projects though virtual site visit in the wake of Covid Pandemic to \nprevent delays in project completion; and (vi) Appointment of District Resource Person in \nParbhani, Washim & Nagpur districts for handholding PMFME applicants;. \n \n(d) & (e): Yes Sir. The details of assistance provided under PMFME scheme, implemented under \nAatmanirbhar Bharat Abhiyan, in Maharashtra State including Washim, Parbhani & Nagpur \ndistricts are placed at Annexure. \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n \n \nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d ) AND  (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 229 FOR ANSWER ON 14 TH DECEMBER, 2021 \nREGARDING SCHEME FOR DEVELOPMENT OF FPIs. \n \nAssistance provided under  PM Formalization of Micro food processing Enterprises \n(PMFME) Scheme in Maharashtra State and Washim, Parbhani & Nagpur districts: \n \nStatus in Maharashtra State \nFinancial Support- \nTotal Micro FPI Units allotted during 5 years \n(2020-21 to 2024-25) \n22234 \nCentral Share released to the state Rs.39.64 crore \nOne District One Product (ODOP) finalized 36 districts \nIncubation Centers approved 2 with an outlay of Rs.  3.98 crore \nSeed Capital  released \n  \nRs.14.90 crore released to 4167 Self Help Group (SHG) \nmembers \nNo of individual entrepreneurs assisted 94 number of loans to individual entrepreneurs have been \nsanctioned. \nTechnical & Commercial Support- \nNo Proposal  approved for Marketing and Branding Support for the state. \n \nState Level Technical Institute has been approved and 21 Master Trainers, 22 District Level Trainers (DLTs), \n48 District Resource Persons (DRPs) and 34 beneficiaries have been trained on EDP and various food domains. \nStatus in Washim, Parbhani & Nagpur districts \nFinancial Support \nIncubation Centers approved 1 (In Nagpur, NOGA Factory, Maharashtra Agro Industries \nDevelopment Cooperation (MIDC) Ltd. has been approved \nas Incubation Centre) \nSeed Capital released \n  \nDistrict Number of \nBeneficiaries \nAmount released to SHG \nmembers (in Lakhs) \nParbhani 31 9.46 \nNagpur 136 46.61  (For the Ramtek region of \nNagpur, amount of Rs. 6.80 Lakh \nhas been disbursed to 17 SHG \nmembers) \nWashim 103 39.98 \n \nNo of individual entrepreneurs assisted District Number of Loans sanctioned \nParbhani 0 \nNagpur 5 \nWashim 6 \n \nTechnical & Commercial Support \nNo Proposal  approved for Marketing and Branding Support \n \nNo District Level trainer DLTs have been appointed in these districts. The details of DRPs are mentioned below: \nDistrict DRP \nParbhani 2 \nNagpur 1 \nWashim 3 \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_23": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n23\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n \n30\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER, 2021\n \n \nCROP DAMAGE DUE TO HEAVY RAINS\n \n \n*23. \n    \nSHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE: \n \n           \nSHRI SUBRAT PATHAK: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n  \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nthe\n \nvalue of agricultural and horticultural crops damaged due to heavy rains in various \nparts of the country during the current rainy season; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the Government has conducted any survey in this regard and if so, the details \nthereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether \nthe Government has received any request from the State Governments for \nproviding assistance to compensate for the loss suffered by farmers and if so, the details \nthereof along with the funds released, State/ UT\n-\nwise; and \n \n \n(d) \n \nthe other steps taken by the\n \nGovernment to cover the loss of life, property and \nlivestock suffered by farmers?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (\n \nd\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the \nHouse.\n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nd\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n23\n  \nDUE FOR REPLY ON\n \n30\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER, 2021\n.\n \n \n(a) to (d):      The State Governments undertake relief measures in the wake of natural \ndisasters from the State \nDisaster Response Fund (SDRF) already placed at their \ndisposal in accordance with Government of India approved items and norms. Additional \nassistance is extended from the National Disaster Response Fund (NDRF) as per \nestablished procedure. The assistance a\npproved under SDRF/NDRF norms is provided \nin the form of relief.\n \n \n             \nApproximately, 50 lakh hectare agricultural area has been affected due to \ncyclonic storm/ flash floods / floods /landslides /cloudburst etc. during 2021, as reported \nby the Stat\ne Governments. Ministry of Home Affairs deputed 19 Inter\n-\nMinisterial Central \nTeams (IMCTs), to 14 States and 02 Union Territories (UTs), as per the details at \nAnnexure.\n \n \n\nANNEXURE\n \n \nAnnexure referred to in \nthe\n \nStatement to \nthe \nLok Sabha\n \nStarred Question \nNo.23 \ndue for answer on 30.11.2021\n \n \n \nState\n-\nwise details of IMCT deputed to assess the damages caused \nby Cyclone, Floods and Landslides during 2021\n \n \n \n \n \nSl. No.\n \nState\n/UT\n \nCalamity\n \n1.\n \nAndhra  Pradesh\n \nFlood 2021\n \n2.\n \nAssam\n \nFlood 2021\n \n3.\n \nBihar\n \nFlood 2021\n \n4.\n \nGujarat\n \nCyclone ‘Tauktae’ of May 2021\n \n5\n.\n \nGoa\n \nCyclone ‘Tauktae’ of May 2021\n \n6\n.\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \nFlood/ landslides of  2021\n \n7\n.\n \nKarnataka\n \n(\ni)  Cyclone ‘Tauktae’ of May 2021\n \n(\nii)  Flood/ landslides of  2021\n \n8\n.\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nFlood 2021\n \n9\n.\n \nMaharashtra\n \n(\ni)   Cyclone ‘Tauktae’ of May 2021\n \n(i\ni)  Flood 2021\n \n10\n.\n \nOdisha\n \nCyclone ‘Yaas’ of 2021\n \n11.\n \nRajasthan\n \nFlood 2021\n \n12.\n \nTamil Nadu\n \nFlood 2021\n \n13.\n \nUttarakhand\n \nFlood/ landslides of  2021\n \n14.\n \nWest Bengal\n \n(\ni)   Cyclone ‘Yaas’ of May 2021\n \n(\nii)  Flood 2021\n \n15\n.\n \nDaman & Diu\n \n(UT)\n \nCyclone ‘Tauktae’ of May 2021\n \n16\n.\n \nPuducherry\n \n(UT)\n \nFlood 2021\n \n \n*****\n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_230": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n MINISTRY OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. *230 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 14.12.2021) \n \nAIR JEYPORE STATION IN ODISHA  \n \n*230.  SHRI SAPTAGIRI SANKAR ULAKA:  \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be plea sed to \nstate:  \n(a)  whether the All India Radio, Jeypore PC station in Odisha has \nbeen included in Bhawanipatna Cluster as per latest directions of \nPrasar Bharati;  \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor;  \n \n(c)  whether the Government is  aware of the discontent in undivided \nKoraput District on the above direction; and  \n\n(d)  the steps taken/being taken by the Government to retain AIR \nJeypore Station in Odisha and make it 3rd Cluster of Odisha? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING; AND \nMINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS  \n(SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR) \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of House. \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *230 FOR ANSWER ON 14.12.2021. \n \n(a) to (d) Prasar Bharati , with the objective of streamlining and \nstrengthening administrative operations across several hundreds of \nsmall field units of DD and AIR spread across India, has consolidated \nadministrative management of DD and AIR establishments into one or \nmore clusters within every state (around 80 clusters across India).  \nAccordingly, the administration of the field units of DD and AIR in the \nstate of Odisha has been organised into three clusters, as per \nAnnexure, each to be headed by a senior offic er who is made \nresponsible for administrative functions of the smaller field units that \nare part of the respective clusters.   \nThis structuring of smaller field units into administrative clusters has \nbeen done to bring operational efficiency  and prudent fi nancial \nmanagement so that service matters, statutory matters such as RTI \nreplies, legal and financial matters of these smaller field units are \nhandled in a timely  and transparent  manner by the senior officer \nheading each cluster.  \n\nThis administrative orga nisation of smaller field units into clusters \nhowever has no bearing on the content operations of AIR Radio \nservice in Jeypore or of any other AIR station in the state of Odisha or \nanywhere in India. \nAIR Jeypore continues to function as before to serve the  needs and \naspirations of the region by delivering radio content in multiple modes \nsuch as on 1467 kHz in Medium Wave, and at 103.6 MHz in FM in \nJeypore, and on “newsOnAir” mobile application on “Android” and \n“iOS” platform for mobile users globally. \n \n\nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a ) to (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *230 FOR ANSWER ON 14.12.2021 \n \nDetails of Clusters in State of Odisha \nCluster Cluster Head Cadre Establishment under cluster \nAIR DD \n1. 2. 3. 4. 5. \n1 Head AIR \nCuttack \nDDG AIR Cuttack, Puri, \nJoranda, Soro, \nBaripada, \nSambhalpur, \nRairangpur, \nKeonjhar, \nRourkela \n \n2 Head DD \nBhubaneswar \nDDG  DDK Bhubneshwar, DDK PGF \nSambhalpur, HPT Berhampur \nHPTV Cuttack, HPT Baleshwar , \nLPTVs at  Baripada, Karanjia, \nKeonjhar, Pallaha ra, Anandpur, \nBhadrak, Durgapur, Talcher , \nAngul, Dhenkanal, Dashrathpur , \nBrajrajnagar, Kuchinda, \nSundergarh, Deogarh, Bonai, \nJoda, Mohana, Banapur, \nParadeep, Rajranapur, \nBhanjanagar, Khandapara, \nBaligurha, Narsinghpur, \nPhulbani, Athamalik, boudh, \nBalangir, Tirtol, Kendrapara. \n3 Head AIR \nBhawanipatna \nwith additional \ncharge of \nHead DD \nBhawanipatna  \nDDG AIR \nBhawanipatna,  \nJeypore, \nBerhampur, \nBolangir \nDDK (PGF) Bhawanipatna , \nLPTVs at  Nuapara, Patnagarh, \nKhariar, Umarkot, Navrangpur, \nPadmpuram, Raiyagada, \nJeypore, Koraput, Simliguda, \nMalkangiri, Parlakhemundi \n ",
