    "ls|LS17_S7_U_34": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 34 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 29.11.2021 \n \nPre-2016 Pensioners \n34 Shri Natarajan P.R.:  \n \n          Will the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n(a) the number of pre -2016 pensioners of higher educational institutions of \nAvinashilingam Higher Studies University at Coimbatore in Tamil Nadu; \n(b) whether the pension arrears of these penserions have not been paid till date;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) the steps taken or proposed to be taken by the Government for the settlement of \npension arrear of these pensioners? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d): The number of pre -2016 pensioners of Avinashilingam Institute for Home \nScience and Higher Education for Women (Deemed to be University), Coimbatore, Tamil \nNadu is 147. The UGC has released an amount of Rs. 800.00 Lakhs as arrears of pension \nto Avinashilingam Institute for Home Science and Higher Education for Women \n(Deemed to be University), Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu during Financial Year 2019-20.  \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_35": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 35 \nANSWERED ON MONDAY, THE 29TH NOVEMBER, 2021 \n[AGRAHAYANA 8, 1943 (SAKA)] \n \nCOMPETITION LAW REVIEW COMMITTEE  \n \nQUESTION \n \n35.  DR. MANOJ RAJORIA:      \n      \n Will the Minister of CORPORATE AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the efforts being made by the Government for better competition laws for \npromoting better mechanism in corporate sector in view of the sharp growth in Indian \neconomy; \n \n(b)  the alternatives suggested in th is regard by the competition law review \ncommittee constituted under the chairmanship of the Secretary, Ministry of Corporate \nAffairs in October, 2018 in this regard; and \n \n(c)  the details of the points reviewed or being reviewed by the committee?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF STATISTICS \nAND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION; MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF PLANNING; AND MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF \nCORPORATE AFFAIRS. \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) to (c): The Government has taken necessary steps for carrying out \nAmendments to the Competition Act, 2002 as and when necessary.  The Competition \nCommission of India (‘Commission’) also has taken action to amend the Regulations \nissued by it from time to time as and when necessary to do so.  S ince the Commission \nbecame functional, there has been a significant growth in Indian markets. The \nCommission has been undertaking various initiatives from time to time to ensure \neffective competition and fair play in the market.  These, inter-alia, include conducting \nmarket studies on relevant sectors, undertaking competition assessment of Model \nConcession Agreements in the infrastructure and other public delivery sectors, \nadvocacy outreach initiatives including State  Resource Person Schemes and \nconducting roadshows on competition laws & practices, upgradation of IT \ninfrastructure and increased use of technology in functioning, opening of regional \noffices, introduction of green channel for certain combination notificat ions, \ncollaboration with other international anti-trust authorities etc.  \n \nThe Competition Law Review Committee (‘Committee’) in its report submitted in July \n2019 had recommended, inter -alia, introduction of ‘settlements & commitments’ \nframework, provision for compounding of certain offences, provision for a green \nchannel for certain combinations notifications, merging of DG office with the \nCommission for greater operational and administrative efficiency, enabling provisions \nto introduce necessary threshold s including  a deal value threshold for merger \nnotifications, etc.  The report of the Committee is available at www.mca.gov.in.  \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_36": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *36 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 30TH NOVEMBER, 2021/ AGRAHAYANA 9, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nNCRB REPORT ON SUICIDES \n \n*36.      SHRI BALUBHAU ALIAS SURESH NARAYAN DHANORKAR: \n    SHRI K. NAVASKANI: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware about recent  NCRB Report, 11,716 \nbusinesspersons died by suicide in 2020, registering a 29% jump from 2019; \n \n(b) whether it is true that the majority of businesspersons who committed \nsuicide belonged to the micro small and medium enterprises (MSMEs); and \n \n(c) if so, the steps taken by the Government to check this trend? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI AJAY KUMAR MISHRA) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n-2- \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN THE REPLY TO THE STARRED QUESTION NO. *36 \nFOR REPLY ON 30 NOVEMBER 2021 \n(a): The National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB) compiles and publishes \nstatistical data on accidents and suicides in its publication “Accidents and \nSuicides in India”. As per the published reports, a total of 9052 business  persons \ncommitted suicide in the year 2019 and a total of 11,716 business  persons \ncommitted suicides in the year 2020. \n(b):  Such an inference may not be possible since the NCRB report does not \ncategorize the suicide data separately for business  persons from micro small \nand medium enterprises (MSMEs).  \n(c)   Does not arise in view of reply to part (b). \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S7_U_37": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF COOPERATION \n \n \nLOK \nSABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n37\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n30\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER\n, 2021\n \n \nSAHAKAR MITRA \n-\n \nNCDC INTERNSHIP SCHEME\n \n \n \n*\n37\n.\n \nSHRI \nVISHNU DAYAL RAM\n \n \n \nWill the Minister of \nCooperation \nसहका\u0000रता\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to s\ntate: \n \n \n(a)\n \nthe details of the Sahakar Mitra \n–\n \nNational Cooperative Development Corporation \n(NCDC) Internship Scheme;\n \n \n(b)\n \nthe list of all the interns who have benefitted from this scheme till date; and\n \n \n(c)\n \nthe details of the funds invested by the Governm\nent to run this scheme?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF \nCOOPERATION\n \n \nसहका\u0000रता\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI \nAMIT SHAH\n)\n \n \n(a) to (c):   \n    \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRE\nD TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c\n) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n37\n \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n30\nTH\n \nNOVEMBER, 2021\n \n \n \n(a)\n:\n \n \nT\nhe details of the \n“\nSAHAKAR MITRA Scheme on Internship Program” \nof National \nCooperative Development Corporation (NCDC) \nis \nenclosed at Annexure\n-\nA. \n \n \n(b)\n:\n \nthe list of all the interns who have benefitted from this scheme till date is \nenclosed at Annexure\n-\nB.\n \n(\nc)\n:\n \nThe \nsaid scheme\n \nis \nneither a Government of India scheme nor funded by the \nGovernment. It is f\nunded \nfrom\n \nits own \nresources\n \nby the NCDC\n.  \n \n \n \n \n\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n37\n \nANNEXURE\n-\nA\n \nThe “SAHAKAR MITRA Scheme on Internship Program” (SIP) is an arrangement where \nNatio\nnal Cooperative Development Corporation (NCDC)\n \nprovide\ns\n \nshort term (not \nexceeding four months) opportunity to young professionals \nto \nacquire learning \nexperience by applying skills and knowledge in organizational context to facilitate \nprofessional developme\nnt as also to lend the benefits of \ntheir \nservices, talent and ideas \nto the Corporation. The programme \nalso \naims at providing an opportunity to \nprofessional graduates to get experience in areas of functioning of NCDC and related \naspects.\n \nA p\nerson with any o\nf the following qualification\ns\n \nis\n \neligible for consideration:\n-\n \ni\n.\n \nProfessional graduat\nes with minimum qualification of\n \nBachelor’s degree in \nAgri\nculture \n/ Dairy\n \n/ Animal Husbandry\n \n/ Veterinary Sciences\n \n/ Fisheries / \nHorticulture\n \n/ Textiles\n \n/ Handloom / IT\n \n(Inf\normation Technology)\n,\n \nduly \nrecommended by the Head of the Department of the UGC / AICTE / ICAR \nrecognized University / Institution as applicable.\n \nii\n.\n \nProfessional (pursuing or completed) MBA \n(\nAgri\ncultural B\nusiness\n)\n \n/ MBA \n(\nCoop\nerative)\n \n/ M.Com\n \n/ MCA / MBA \n(\nFina\nnce\n) \n/ MBA \n(\nInternational Trade\n)\n \n/ \nMBA \n(\nForestry\n) \n/ MBA \n(\nRural Dev\nelopment)\n \n/ MBA \n(\nProject Management\n)\n \n/ \nInter\nmediate\n \nICAI / \nInter\nmediate\n \nICWA\n,\n \nqualification duly recommended by \nthe Head of the Department of the UGC / AICTE / ICAR recognized University \n/ I\nnstitution as applicable.\n \nThe details and guidelines of the scheme is available\n \nat the portal \nhttp://sip.ncdc.in\n \n \n.\n \n\nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 37\n \nANNEXURE\n-\nB\n \nS.No.\n \nName of Intern\n \nPlace of Internship\n \nDuration\n \n1\n \nMr. Na\ndikuda Ravi Kiran\n \nHyderabad\n \n01.09.2020 to 31.12.2020\n \n2\n \nMr. M. S. Keerthana\n \nBengaluru\n \n01.09.2020 to 31.12.2020\n \n3\n \nMs. Shruti Shukla\n \nLucknow\n \n01.09.2020 to 31.12.2020\n \n4\n \nMr. Bishnu Shankar Mishra\n \nLucknow\n \n01.09.2020 to 31.12.2020\n \n5\n \nMr. Tushar Virmani\n \nLINAC\n-\nG\nurugram\n \n01.09.2020 to 31.12.2020\n \n6\n \nMr. Nitin Azad\n \nShimla\n \n01.09.2020 to 31.12.2020\n \n7\n \nMr. Sattwick Das\n \nBhubaneswar\n \n01.09.2020 to 31.12.